== Nonlinear and Higher-Order Extensions ==

The linear constitutive relation <math>P_\psi = \varepsilon_0\chi_\psi\psi</math> is the leading-order approximation valid for small ψ amplitudes. For large-amplitude fields (e.g., inside a [[ψ Resonator]] at high Q, or during group coherence amplification), nonlinear terms appear:

:<math>P_\psi = \varepsilon_0\!\left[\chi_\psi^{(1)}\psi + \chi_\psi^{(2)}\psi^2 + \chi_\psi^{(3)}\psi^3 + \ldots\right]</math>

The <math>\chi_\psi^{(3)}</math> term is of particular interest: it is the ψ analogue of the nonlinear optical susceptibility <math>\chi^{(3)}</math> that governs self-focusing and four-wave mixing in nonlinear optics. In the psionic context, <math>\chi_\psi^{(3)}</math> contributes an additional <math>\psi^3</math> term to the wave equation — adding to the existing <math>\lambda\psi^3</math> self-interaction term from the master equation. The combined nonlinear coefficient becomes:

:<math>\lambda_{\rm eff} = \lambda + \varepsilon_0\chi_\psi^{(3)}</math>

This means that a material with large <math>\chi_\psi^{(3)}</math> effectively enhances the nonlinear soliton-supporting capability of the composite. Whether the BST phase or the PZT-5H phase contributes a significant <math>\chi_\psi^{(3)}</math> is a TML-3 measurement question.

== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== Biological Tissue Constitutive Relations ===

The most important entry in the master material parameter table is biological cortical tissue — the primary operator interface. Within the ψ hypothesis (Track B), coherent neural firing patterns determine the spatial and temporal structure of <math>J_\psi^{\rm (src)}</math> (from [[ψ Conservation Laws]] A2 and [[Psionics]]). The constitutive parameters of cortical tissue — <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math>, <math>\varepsilon_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math>, and <math>\mu_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math> — determine how the operator's self-generated ψ field propagates through their own brain tissue.

If <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math> is large (highly ψ-responsive tissue), the brain effectively acts as a ψ metamaterial that shapes and focuses its own ψ output. Training — the development of sustained HRV coherence and cortical synchrony — may correspond physically to increasing <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math> through neuroplastic changes in the tissue's effective susceptibility.

This hypothesis is Track B and requires TML-3 confirmation. However, the constitutive relation framework established on this page provides the mathematical language for stating it precisely and for designing experiments to test it.

=== Consciousness-Dependent χ_ψ ===

The most speculative extension: if <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math> depends on the operator's attentional state — increasing during focused intention and decreasing during mind-wandering — then the constitutive relation itself becomes time-dependent:

:<math>P_\psi(t) = \varepsilon_0\,\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}(t)\,\psi(t)</math>

where <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}(t)</math> is driven by the neural state. This would make the brain a time-varying ψ metamaterial — a material whose properties change on the timescale of attention shifts (~1–10 seconds). The [[HRV-Gated Drive]] (D5) Mk2.0 loop estimates the current value of <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}(t)</math> via RMSSD as a proxy and adjusts the device's impedance match accordingly.

== TML Measurement Protocol ==

=== TML-1 — Null Material Verification and Composite Characterisation ===

'''Step 1 — Null material baseline:''' Measure the VNA S-parameter response of an air-gap coaxial fixture (no material). Record resonant frequencies and Q values. This establishes the null material (<math>\chi_\psi = 0</math>) reference.

'''Step 2 — Material sample measurement:''' Insert composite sample (10 mm × 10 mm × 2 mm tablet from B7+B8 protocol) into the fixture. Remeasure S11, S21. Apply Nicholson–Ross–Weir extraction to recover complex <math>\varepsilon_\psi(\omega)</math> and <math>\mu_\psi(\omega)</math> from 1 kHz to 1 MHz.

'''Step 3 — Consistency check:''' Verify Kramers–Kronig consistency on extracted parameters. If violated, the measurement has systematic errors (likely fixture calibration issues — recheck SOLT calibration).

'''Pass criteria:''' Measurement reproducible across three samples from same batch to within ±15%. Kramers–Kronig consistency confirmed. If any material shows <math>\varepsilon_\psi \neq \varepsilon_0</math> or <math>\mu_\psi \neq \mu_0</math> at > 3σ statistical confidence, the null material assumption is falsified for that material — a significant result warranting detailed follow-up.

=== TML-3 — Biological Interface Measurement ===

TML-3 is required for the biological tissue rows of the master table. Protocol:

# Operator wears [[Psi Stabilizer]] in Standby mode (no emission). Device acts as a passive sensor only.
# OPM magnetometer array records fields at the shell surface during baseline HRV state and peak HRV coherence state (achieved by HeartMath coherence breathing protocol).
# Difference in shell resonant frequency between baseline and coherence states provides an estimate of <math>\Delta\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math>.
# Requires [[ψ Falsifiability Framework]] (F1) sham-controlled design — see [[Sham Control Design]] (F2).

